{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "4d81d2fc-2dda-5528-8e9a-8417c8b0ca79",
  "Description": "A bowl is carved out of a block with volume CSG, and the balls collect in it.\n\n[VolumeCsg] subtracts a sphere from a box, both made by [VolumePrimitive]. The result is meshed by [VolumeToMesh] and used as a static collider, so editing the volumes edits what the balls collide with.\n\nAKA: csg, boolean, carve, crater, destruction, level set collider\n\nTips\n- Move the sphere's Center to carve a different crater; the collider follows when the volume changes.\n- Operation on [VolumeCsg]: Union adds the sphere as a dome, Intersection keeps only the overlap.\n- For rendering alone, the same shape is cheaper as an SDF field with [CombineSDF]; the volume is needed here because physics runs on the CPU.",
